# Include IFSMHP Orchestrator & Stage Agents

Before editing, testing, reviewing, creating/merging PRs, or deploying this project, follow the **IFSMHP Agentic SDLC Pipeline** governed by `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-orchestrator.md` and `.cursor/skills/ifsmhp-sdlc-pipeline/SKILL.md`.

## Master Orchestrator & Connected Skills

| Role | Artifact |
|---|---|
| **End-to-End Agentic Workflow Spec** | `docs/agentic-workflow.md` |
| **Master Supervisor / Flow Controller** | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-orchestrator.md` |
| **SDLC Pipeline Skill & Handoff Contracts** | `.cursor/skills/ifsmhp-sdlc-pipeline/SKILL.md` + `CONTRACTS.md` |
| **Local Runtime & Operations Skill** | `.cursor/skills/ifsmhp-operate/SKILL.md` |

## Sequential Pipeline Subagents (Stage 1 → Stage 8)

Execute stages sequentially via `ifsmhp-orchestrator`. Every stage returns a structured `handoff_envelope` verified by the orchestrator before advancing:

| Order | Stage | Agent | Mode |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1** | Development Coding | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-development.md` | Read/Write |
| **2** | Unit & Integration Testing | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-unit-test.md` | Read/Write |
| **3** | Code Review | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-code-review.md` | `readonly` |
| **4** | Security Audit (`R1`–`R5`, `I.1`–`I.17`) | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-security.md` | `readonly` |
| **5** | Pull Request Creation | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-pr-creator.md` | Read/Write |
| **6** | Pull Request Validation | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-pr-validator.md` | `readonly` |
| **7** | Pull Request Merge | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-pr-merger.md` | Read/Write (explicit merge request only) |
| **8** | Production Deployment | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-deployment.md` | Read/Write (explicit deploy request only) |

## Operational Specialists (Invoked by Orchestrator / Stage 8)

| Work | Read first |
|---|---|
| Configure, run, test, database, or API deploy | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-operator.md` |
| Frontend build or Hostinger publish | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-frontend-release.md` |
| PR merge, deployment, or hosting verification | `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-release-verifier.md` |

Read every agent whose work the change touches. On any `FAIL` in Stages 2–4 or 6, loop back to Stage 1 (`ifsmhp-development`) and re-verify from Stage 2. Stop after Stage 6 (validated PR) unless the user asked to merge or deploy. After any deploy or PR merge, run `.cursor/agents/ifsmhp-release-verifier.md` before calling the work done.

Work as a senior engineer: keep the change small, do not commit secrets or unrelated dirty files, prove the result with a test or a live check, and do not claim a release is complete until the verifier passes.

Ask the user only before a critical change: deleting or resetting production data, changing the `www`, `@`, or `ftp` DNS records, replacing a working certificate, opening a new public port, or touching any server other than the `ifsmhp` instance.
